{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## DUPLICATE of [rebar:aec1-76e7-bb95-4c86] — that is the work ticket; this one's MECHANISM is the better half\n\nFiled within minutes of each other for the same defect: I filed aec1 from the symptom (the c827\ncontrol-group question could not be answered from the store), and the c827 investigation filed this\none having found the actual cause. **aec1 is claimed and being implemented — work continues there.**\n\n**This ticket's mechanism is the valuable part and has been handed to that implementation**, because\nit converts a hypothesis into two concrete, testable defects:\n\n* `usage_log.record()` **no-ops unless `REBAR_USAGE_LOG` is set** — unset by default, and unset here.\n  So the recording code exists and is inert.\n* `_FIELDS` (`usage_log.py:32`) records `requests` but **NOT `tool_calls`** — the one axis that\n  separates a loop from genuine breadth, and the second of the two kill paths.\n\nThat is the same **computed-then-discarded** shape as its siblings — the repetition diagnostic built\nby `interpret_failure` and dropped because `failure_diagnostic is None`, and the deterministic\nchild-closure proof collapsed to a boolean before it reaches the prompt\n([rebar:6ec8-24c7-182b-40d0]). Three instances of one pattern in one subsystem.\n\nLeft open rather than closed: closing it needs the gates, and the honest disposition is `duplicate`\nnaming aec1 as the live replacement — which is exactly the disposition-attestation path\n[rebar:738a-376e-4829-42ca] fixed earlier in this epic. Recording the relationship now so neither\nticket is worked twice."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785947378949109001,"uuid":"a4fe231f-a1e3-4482-8f1a-72812072c95c"}